                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b9168168-65ae-46be-8c98-466990007522",
                        "source_entry_id": "d668f069-9927-3575-8ccc-77a07ef61c6b",
                        "source_sense_id": "4d328dca-c84b-36d4-94dc-1ae9db4c90c0",
                        "target_lang_word": "methyl",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "methyl",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff6af3ec-8b6d-309c-bfcd-55f0437d6465",
                                        "entry_id": "2f5c62f7-c224-33c7-9fc6-2c86270db1e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The univalent hydrocarbon radical, CH₃-, formally derived from methane by the loss of a hydrogen atom; a compound or part of a compound formed by the attachment of such a radical."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e4791ab-e501-43bf-94f4-c9c975512640",
                                                "sense_id": "ff6af3ec-8b6d-309c-bfcd-55f0437d6465",
                                                "text": "You might point out in the theory of oxidation of oils, in development of rancidity in oils, that many methyls accelerate this oxidation of oils. I do not want to burden you with a lecture on chemistry but there are some methyls like iron which has both a valence of two and of three. Another example is cobalt which has a valence of both two and three."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06b4c382-2b44-497e-8a10-e5a1d04d4bf4",
                                                "sense_id": "ff6af3ec-8b6d-309c-bfcd-55f0437d6465",
                                                "text": "The southern acetates must be decarboxylated to methyls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62427a45-196f-41b3-a9f1-2b6e990f6f52",
                                                "sense_id": "ff6af3ec-8b6d-309c-bfcd-55f0437d6465",
                                                "text": "The most stable form has the groups staggered and the methyls as far from each other as possible (DA^([dihedral angle]) = 180°)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6043bfc9-f7ad-400f-96d0-7c8e27ffc326",
                        "source_entry_id": "d668f069-9927-3575-8ccc-77a07ef61c6b",
                        "source_sense_id": "4d328dca-c84b-36d4-94dc-1ae9db4c90c0",
                        "target_lang_word": "méthyle",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "méthyle",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f792a2fc-0daa-3a62-b3d7-e64904cab1be",
                                        "entry_id": "e439a86b-89e5-3138-935d-0575c77bb72e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Groupement de carbone et d’hydrogène de structure (CH₃–) dérivé de la structure du méthane et lié de façon covalente à une autre molécule, et entrant dans la composition d'une foule de composés organiques."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Chimie organique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9996f85c-321f-4054-b269-a3b7783bba97",
                                                "sense_id": "f792a2fc-0daa-3a62-b3d7-e64904cab1be",
                                                "text": "C’est ainsi que le méthylarsonite de sodium réagit sous cette seconde forme, avec l’iodure de méthyle, pour donner le diméthylarsinate de sodium."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34f834e7-8144-4825-8663-ada6b6fc9143",
                                                "sense_id": "f792a2fc-0daa-3a62-b3d7-e64904cab1be",
                                                "text": "On évitera de préférence en culture maraîchère les nématicides contenant du brome, comme le dibromoéthane ou le bromure de méthyle ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65dc8016-06fb-4796-94d5-45ce0a14597b",
                                                "sense_id": "f792a2fc-0daa-3a62-b3d7-e64904cab1be",
                                                "text": "Le chlorure de méthyle est un gaz qui, liquéfié, sert de frigorifique et d’anesthésique."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
